# Ordinary report preparation and geometry prefix correction

This is a Source-only proposal. Nothing here has been applied, formatted, built,
or executed. Root authorized diagnosis after the accepted comparison reported
829 discrete mismatches. The complete failing evidence remains unchanged.

The production lane accounts for 762 mismatches: 54 first-scan owner differences
and 708 full predefined-table differences. The latter are six missing surface
film-U entries followed by shifted construction-layer entries. The direct lane's
67 differences are a separate Header-owned proposal. No comparer or policy is
changed by this package, and no observed Native value becomes a Rust input or
test expectation.

EnergyPlusData::init_state first runs GetProjectData, then CheckIfAnyEMS.
CheckIfAnyEMS performs the EnergyManagementSystem query even with no active EMS;
that first query populates all five report families before BeforeRegistry.
The new context preparation uses the accepted fallible Scan implementation and
the actual backend. Its existing GetReportInput owner prevents a second query
after the production observer prepares before its before-snapshot. A supplied
prescanned owner is retained, rather than relabelled as a newly reached query.
The selected no-EMS requested-EDD warning/continue suffix is also retained.
This does not implement active EMS, external HVAC/API mode, or GetProjectData.

The ordinary initializer performs genuine registration, then the geometry
report predecessor, then the existing construction cache/Init/postlude chain.
The new geometry helper follows SurfaceGeometry's actual Zone/Space/base-class
order. The existing compiler already registers the represented opaque surfaces
in that order; no observed surface permutation is supplied as an input. All
typed surfaces must be represented once. Outdoors uses exterior film0.0299387;
Adiabatic resolves to the same surface and its own class film. Ceiling uses the
actual Roof class. Other boundaries remain typed unavailable in this port.

Material::GetMaterialData assigns Regular Resistance and NominalR together and
copies NoMass input resistance to NominalR. GetConstructData adds those values
in outside-to-inside layer order, initializes NominalU to zero, and assigns1/R
only when R is nonzero. ComputeNominalUwithConvCoeffs retains the subsequent
reciprocal and its exact addition order. The helper copies those operations;
it does not substitute the existing runtime's aggregate thermal resistance or
CTF-derived UValue. Unread unsupported material declarations remain unread;
a referenced unsupported material stops the reached producer.

The real three-decimal predefined entry reuses the existing allocation/count
and common string writes, then stores origRealEntry/significantDigits/real flag.
It retains preceding entries, all allocated tails, and untouched members. Only
the finite fixed-format branch is represented; values requiring scientific or
nonfinite formatting are explicit unavailable. The selected positive films
bound ordinary positive U far below that branch boundary. The existing accepted
fmt8 F helper supplies the text; no second formatter is introduced.

Six unexecuted focused tests cover order/space ownership, complete table prefix
and tail retention, class/boundary films and real column IDs, stored loader-R
and zero NominalU, unused versus referenced unsupported material, excluded or
unregistered surfaces, and the shared first-scan/cache boundary. These are
authored input owners and Source behavior checks, not Native output fixtures.

There are eight application rows: six exact current-before files and two absent
destinations. Header's three direct observer files are disjoint. The production
observer's own4 order is unchanged; its API order adds the executable geometry
module and is explicitly59 in runtime_interfaces. Tests remain covered by the
future full raw Source snapshot. Runtime hashes/receipts, formatting, quality,
candidate execution, and comparison are future Root-owned actions. No CTF gate,
whole-engine integration claim, or numerical PASS is inferred from this hold.
